WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.032
Priya: Approve a capacity pilot for reports. Isolated tests first, one region afterward.

2
00:00:07.032 --> 00:00:14.015
Hannah: Which tenants represent the actual skew? A tiny tenant isn't a useful pilot.

3
00:00:14.015 --> 00:00:19.463
Anika: One large and two smaller tenants. I'm on it with the feature switch.

4
00:00:19.463 --> 00:00:25.847
Raj: The full table scan should shrink selectively. Broad reports may still scan reasonably.

5
00:00:25.847 --> 00:00:32.926
Lukas: Compare against the peak load baseline. Include transaction latency beside report improvements.

6
00:00:32.926 --> 00:00:40.390
Priya: Just to confirm, identical totals required, right? Faster wrong reports fail the pilot.

7
00:00:40.390 --> 00:00:48.477
Hannah: Yes. Lower disk reads are another gate. Keep transaction latency below two hundred.

8
00:00:48.477 --> 00:00:55.389
Anika: Incorrect totals are the immediate rollback trigger. Maybe scan savings vary by date range.

9
00:00:55.389 --> 00:01:02.276
Lukas: And sustained write regression halts expansion. Revert the query switch, preserve evidence.

10
00:01:02.276 --> 00:01:09.140
Raj: Okay, order storage for all nodes now. Pilot success won't postpone that preparation.

